{"tool_name":"bcheck_rnpb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"bcheck_rnpb","home":"http://rna.tbi.univie.ac.at/bcheck/index.html","summary":"Wrapper tool for rnpB gene prediction by combining speed of rnabob descriptor model and sensitivity of infernal covariance model.","addition_date":"2016-01-19T13:36:04Z","last_update_date":"2019-03-12T13:07:30Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Database portal","Web application"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bcheck_rnpb","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"dilmurat.yusuf@gmail.com","name":"Dilmurat Yusuf","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-8683-7845","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"],"url":"http://bioinformatics.mdc-berlin.de/team.html#dilmurat-yusuf-phd"},{"email":"dilmurat.yusuf@gmail.com","name":"Dilmurat Yusuf","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-8683-7845","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://bioinformatics.mdc-berlin.de/team.html#dilmurat-yusuf-phd"},{"name":"Ivo Hofacker","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7132-0800","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Austrian GEN-AU projects \"bioinformatics integration network III\"","typeEntity":"Funding agency","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Institute for Theoretical Chemistry","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"rnateam","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://rna.tbi.univie.ac.at/bcheck/help.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"DNA sequence (raw)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3497"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}],"note":"Services on Bcheck rnpB server:  Online rnpB gene prediction with Bcheck; Database comprising rnpB genes predicted by Bcheck;  BLAST search our database Genomic or any DNA sequences in FASTA format. Output provides RNAse P RNA (rnpB) sequences in fasta format.","operation":[{"term":"Genetic code prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0489"},{"term":"Genome annotation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0362"},{"term":"Sequence database search (by property)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0349"},{"term":"Sequence similarity search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0346"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"RNA sequence (raw)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3496"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"Bcheck rnpB server","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"rnateam","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2164-11-432","metadata":{"abstract":"Background: Effective bioinformatics solutions are needed to tackle challenges posed by industrial-scale genome annotation. We present Bcheck, a wrapper tool which predicts RNase P RNA genes by combining the speed of pattern matching and sensitivity of covariance models. The core of Bcheck is a library of subfamily specific descriptor models and covariance models.Results: Scanning all microbial genomes in GenBank identifies RNase P RNA genes in 98% of 1024 microbial chromosomal sequences within just 4 hours on single CPU. Comparing to existing annotations found in 387 of the GenBank files, Bcheck predictions have more intact structure and are automatically classified by subfamily membership. For eukaryotic chromosomes Bcheck could identify the known RNase P RNA genes in 84 out of 85 metazoan genomes and 19 out of 21 fungi genomes. Bcheck predicted 37 novel eukaryotic RNase P RNA genes, 32 of which are from fungi. Gene duplication events are observed in at least 20 metazoan organisms. Scanning of meta-genomic data from the Global Ocean Sampling Expedition, comprising over 10 million sample sequences (18 Gigabases), predicted 2909 unique genes, 98% of which fall into ancestral bacteria A type of RNase P RNA and 66% of which have no close homolog to known prokaryotic RNase P RNA.Conclusions: The combination of efficient filtering by means of a descriptor-based search and subsequent construction of a high-quality gene model by means of a covariance model provides an efficient method for the detection of RNase P RNA genes in large-scale sequencing data.Bcheck is implemented as webserver and can also be downloaded for local use from http://rna.tbi.univie.ac.at/bcheck. \u00a9 2010 Yusuf et al; licensee BioMed Central Ltd.","authors":[{"name":"Hofacker I.L."},{"name":"Marz M."},{"name":"Stadler P.F."},{"name":"Yusuf D."}],"citationCount":25,"date":"2010-07-13T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Genomics","title":"Bcheck: A wrapper tool for detecting RNase P RNA genes"},"pmcid":"PMC2996960","pmid":"20626900","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Gene structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0114"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Bcheck rnpB server","home":"https://bio.tools/bcheck_rnpb","summary":"Wrapper tool for rnpB gene prediction by combining speed of rnabob descriptor model and sensitivity of infernal covariance model.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:bcheck_rnpb/cmd/rna.tbi.univie.ac.at","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":15,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2010"},{"count":1,"year":"2011"},{"count":1,"year":"2018"},{"count":2,"year":"2013"},{"count":2,"year":"2014"},{"count":2,"year":"2020"},{"count":3,"year":"2015"},{"count":3,"year":"2017"}],"doi":"10.1186/1471-2164-11-432","pmcid":"PMC2996960","pmid":"20626900","ref_count":43,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"-1"},{"count":1,"year":"1983"},{"count":1,"year":"1988"},{"count":1,"year":"1990"},{"count":1,"year":"1996"},{"count":1,"year":"1999"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"count":2,"year":"1997"},{"count":